commit 20e8d5f6fe34cfe888b96c922da8b7b1ebf07519
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 4 07:31:58 2026 +0000

    CI-1b: the stub journals an exit before its state lets the position go
    
    Root cause of the tabletop/recovered_state failure seen once under full-suite load: the
    stub saved its state without the position, then journaled the exit. A SIGKILL between the
    two writes (a descheduled process under load) left a state without the position and a
    journal without its exit, so the runner, from a reply that showed the position, expected
    it back and failed recovered_state. Reproduced every time with a test hook that stalls the
    stub 2.5 s between the two writes (ZEROED_STUB_EXIT_GAP_MS) and a crash falling due in
    the stall. The exit line is now written first: a kill between the writes leaves a state
    holding more than the journal says, never less (entries already save state first).
    ARCHITECTURE §12.4 states the write order for every worker.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VgCLpHWaM7FjpwofRcgrwM

